<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="throw_radial.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="throw_radial">
    <!-- Throw quick-slot radial (ACTION_THROW_QUICKSLOT).

         Opened PASSIVE: it paints over the world every frame but never captures
         input, so throw_radial.cpp owns the whole interaction (mouse direction,
         1-6, ENTER, ESC, and hold-to-release). That matters because the pointer
         is sampled every tick rather than on click — RmlUi hover would only fire
         on real mouse events, and hold-mode needs to track the cursor while the
         player is holding a key and not clicking at all.

         Every slot is absolutely positioned from C++ (throw_radial_apply_rect):
         RCSS has no trigonometry, so the ring is laid out in the controller and
         the stylesheet only owns appearance. Slots carry a negative half-size
         margin so the C++ side can anchor each one by its CENTRE and stay pure
         trig — see the note in throw_radial.rcss. -->
    <div id="tr-scrim"></div>
    <div id="tr-ring">
        <div class="tr-slot" id="tr-slot-0">
            <div class="tr-key" data-rml="s0_key"></div>
            <div class="tr-name" data-rml="s0_name"></div>
            <div class="tr-count" data-rml="s0_count"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="tr-slot" id="tr-slot-1">
            <div class="tr-key" data-rml="s1_key"></div>
            <div class="tr-name" data-rml="s1_name"></div>
            <div class="tr-count" data-rml="s1_count"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="tr-slot" id="tr-slot-2">
            <div class="tr-key" data-rml="s2_key"></div>
            <div class="tr-name" data-rml="s2_name"></div>
            <div class="tr-count" data-rml="s2_count"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="tr-slot" id="tr-slot-3">
            <div class="tr-key" data-rml="s3_key"></div>
            <div class="tr-name" data-rml="s3_name"></div>
            <div class="tr-count" data-rml="s3_count"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="tr-slot" id="tr-slot-4">
            <div class="tr-key" data-rml="s4_key"></div>
            <div class="tr-name" data-rml="s4_name"></div>
            <div class="tr-count" data-rml="s4_count"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="tr-slot" id="tr-slot-5">
            <div class="tr-key" data-rml="s5_key"></div>
            <div class="tr-name" data-rml="s5_name"></div>
            <div class="tr-count" data-rml="s5_count"></div>
        </div>
        <!-- Hub: names the current selection so the choice is readable without
             having to track which of six cards is lit. -->
        <div id="tr-hub">
            <div id="tr-hub-title" data-rml="hub_title"></div>
            <div id="tr-hub-sel" data-rml="hub_sel"></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
